"r1bQkb1r/ppp2ppp/2p5/4Pn2/8/5N2/PPP2PPP/RNB2RK1 b kq -":{"variation":"berlin-defence","moves":[{"uci":"e8d8","notes":[{"text":"You lead in development and Black can't castle, but your e5 pawn is weak. Good moves: Rd1+, h3, Nc3.","original":"This one of the most theoretical openings in all of chess. White has castled and has a clear lead in development., but the e pawn is a weakness right now. As for black, he has reduced most of the tension, but black still needs to develop and he has forfeited castling rights. What black wants to do is get some initiative with his light-squared bishop and develop as soon as possible. White has 3 good moves, (in order of popularity) Rd1+, h3, & Nc3."}]}]},
"r1bq1rk1/4bppp/p2p1n2/npp1p3/4P3/2P2N1P/PPBP1PP1/RNBQR1K1 w - -":{"variation":"closed-ruy-lopez-chigorin-variation","moves":[{"uci":"d2d4","book":true,"notes":[{"text":"Your d4 challenges the center, hitting c5 and e5, the move you have prepared all along.","original":"White doesn't allow for the knight to get back to c6 and plays d4 right away. The move d4 challenges the center and is basically the move that white has been preparing to play all along.","ideas":[{"type":"purpose","from":"d4","relation":"attacks","targets":["c5","e5"]}]}]}]},
